# Integration test environment (copy to .env.test.local — never commit secrets)
#
# Setup:
# 1. Create an empty local database named ose_inventory_test.
# 2. Copy this file to .env.test.local and add local credentials.
# 3. Run npm run test:integration:bootstrap once.
# 4. Run npm run test:integration.
#    The suite includes Wave 1B proof, Wave 2A ACC permission resolution, Wave 2B assignment scope characterization, and Wave 2C JWT permission-version freshness.
# 5. The bootstrap uses prisma db push only.
# 6. It does not validate migration history.
# 7. SF-004 remains open until the migration chain is repaired.
#
# Test-only JWT secrets (not production). Copy into .env.test.local with local DB credentials.
JWT_SECRET=local-test-access-secret
JWT_REFRESH_SECRET=local-test-refresh-secret
NODE_ENV=test
OSE_TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@127.0.0.1:5433/ose_inventory_test
